            <ArticleTitle>The twin block: a simple technique to block both the masseteric and the anterior deep temporal nerves with one anesthetic injection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e65-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.oooo.2014.01.227</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2212-4403(14)00260-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The objective of this article is to describe a new technique to anesthetize the masseter muscle and the temporalis muscle using a single extraoral approach. The block targets both the masseteric and the deep temporal nerves as they leave the infratemporal fossa to innervate the deep surfaces of their respective muscles.</AbstractText>
